  TWO CONTROLS, read them before the raw alignment.
  null    CKA after permuting the token index on the supply side. Both Grams
          have magnitude-dominated diagonals, so unrelated Grams score high
          for trivial reasons. Only alignment MINUS null is signal.
  reach%  fraction of the demand a linear router could even in principle
          predict from x. The rest is minibatch and label noise that inflates
          the spectrum and offers nothing to condition on. If this is small,
          there is no headroom for ANY x-conditioned design and the measured
          demand was never the opportunity it looked like.

  Read it this way. A plain linear projection has J_t = W for every token,
  so it supplies zero operator variation and its entire demand is unmet.
  An FFN supplies variation for free because it is nonlinear. Where alignment
  is high the free variation already points where the gradients pull, and no
  conditioning scheme can add anything there at any price. Where alignment is
  low there is room, and the cheap way to buy it is more nonlinearity per FLOP
  (depth multiplies linear regions, width only adds them), not more parameters.

