==============================================================================
HOW TO READ THIS
==============================================================================
  headroom  fraction of the per-token weight-gradient signal that a single
            static operator cannot represent. This is the ceiling on what
            ANY input-conditioned design can win at that layer, before
            architecture, routing or optimization enter the picture.
  dof       independent directions the tokens disagree along. Compare to
            K-1 for a template bank and to R for ConditionedLinear. Biased
            low by 1/(1 + dof/N); at N=4096 a true value of 64 reads as
            63.
  top1      share of the dispersion in its leading direction. Near 1 means
            the disagreement is essentially rank-1.

  model-wide: headroom 0.9907, dof 175.3
  => there is real headroom. Size K or R against the per-layer dof column
     rather than uniformly, and spend nothing where headroom is ~0.

